# fastly_bot_management_category_overrides_clear Action

Clears the bot overrides in a Bot Management (ContentGuard) category. Every bot
with its own action is set back to `inherit`, so it uses the category's action.
The category's own action is unchanged.

## Example Usage

```terraform
data "fastly_bot_management_workspace" "example" {
  service_id = fastly_service_cdn_auto.example.id
}

resource "fastly_bot_management_category" "ai_crawler" {
  workspace_id = data.fastly_bot_management_workspace.example.id
  category_id  = "cat_ai_crawler"
  action       = "block"
}

action "fastly_bot_management_category_overrides_clear" "ai_crawler" {
  config {
    workspace_id = data.fastly_bot_management_workspace.example.id
    category_id  = fastly_bot_management_category.ai_crawler.category_id
  }
}
```

```shell
terraform apply -invoke=action.fastly_bot_management_category_overrides_clear.ai_crawler
```

## Usage Notes

This also clears the overrides of bots managed by `fastly_bot_management_bot`.
The next `apply` sets their configured actions again, so set those resources to
`inherit` or remove them first if the overrides should stay cleared.

